OT.append(U(CH, 'Mehterhane', [M('Army Bandsman', '4 3 3 3 3 2 4 1 8', 20, weapons=['Hand Weapon', 'Light Armour'], rules=['Kapikulu', 'Mehterhane', 'Camels'], options=[('Ride a horse', 0), ('Ride a camel (+12 pts)', 12), ('Cloth barding', 4), ('Heavy armour (replaces light armour)', 2), ('Partial plate armour, if mounted (replaces light armour)', 2), ('Partial plate armour, if dismounted (replaces light armour)', 4)])],
    'Hand weapon, light armour, and musical instrument. Must have a horse (free) or camel (+12 pts) if mounted. Mounts may have cloth barding (+4 pts). May wear heavy armour (+2 pts) or partial plate armour (+2 pts if mounted, +4 pts if dismounted). Kapikulu. Mehterhane: if used, Mehterhane models must be deployed together and with the Army General; the unit led by the General and including the band is immune to panic, and each Mehterhane model in the unit adds +1" to the Leadership radius of the Army General up to a maximum of +4". If taken, Camels. Ottoman Empire only: 0-4 Mehterhane (0-2 in armies of up to 1,999 pts, 0-3 in armies from 2,000 to 2,999 pts, and 0-4 from 3,000 pts and up; only the maximum of four is enforced).', mx=4, page='39'))
